<title>SINGAPORE: CompuServe opens Singapore online service.</title>
<headline>CompuServe opens Singapore online service.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S.-based CompuServe Corp, said on Wednesday it had launched its online services in Singapore through a partnership with SingNet, a Singapore Internet Service Provider (ISP).</p>
<p>The CompuServe service, distributed in Singapore by Fujitsu Australia Ltd, allows SingNet subscribers to access the Internet from more than 185 countries for A$19.50 a month.</p>
<p>SingNet is part of state-owned telephone company Singapore Telecom.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
